<#GAPDoc Label="DotDigraph">
  <ManSection>
    <Attr Name="DotDigraph" Arg="D"/>
    <Attr Name="DotSymmetricDigraph" Arg="D"/>
    <Returns>A string.</Returns>
    <Description>
      <B>WARNING!</B> As of v2.0.0 of &Digraphs; these functions are
      deprecated in favour of:
      <List>
          <Item><Ref Oper="GraphvizDigraph"/></Item>
          <Item><Ref Oper="GraphvizGraph"/></Item>
      </List>
      They return the strings
      <C>AsString(GraphvizDigraph(<A>D</A>))</C> and
      <C>AsString(GraphvizGraph(<A>D</A>))</C>, respectively.
      <C>DotSymmetricDigraph</C> requires <A>D</A> to be symmetric.
    </Description>
  </ManSection>
<#/GAPDoc>

<#GAPDoc Label="GraphvizDigraph">
  <ManSection>
    <Oper Name="GraphvizDigraph" Arg="D"/>
    <Oper Name="GraphvizGraph" Arg="D"/>
    <Returns>A &GRAPHVIZFORGAP; object.</Returns>
    <Description>
      <Ref Oper="GraphvizDigraph"/> and <Ref Oper="GraphvizGraph"/> return
      mutable &GAP; objects representing graphviz objects, which provide a
      flexible means of tailoring pictures of graphs and digraphs to your
      needs.
      <P/>

      <C>GraphvizDigraph</C> and <C>GraphvizGraph</C> produce &GRAPHVIZFORGAP;
      objects representing the digraph <A>D</A>. Vertices are displayed as
      circles, numbered consistently with <A>D</A>. For <C>GraphvizDigraph</C>,
      edges are displayed as arrowed lines between vertices, with the arrowhead
      of each line pointing towards the range of the edge. For
      <C>GraphvizGraph</C>, edges are displayed without an arrowhead.
      <C>GraphvizGraph</C> requires <A>D</A> to be symmetric; see
      <Ref Prop="IsSymmetricDigraph"/>.
      <P/>

      To display the result, use
      <Ref Func="Splash" BookName="GraphvizForGAP"/>. Its documentation
      describes the optional record controlling the output directory,
      filename, viewer, rendering engine, and file type.
      <Log><![CDATA[
gap> Splash(GraphvizDigraph(D));
]]></Log>
      To write the Graphviz source to a file, use
      <C>FileString("digraph.dot", AsString(GraphvizDigraph(D)))</C>;
      see <Ref Func="FileString" BookName="GAPDoc"/>.
      <P/>

      <Example><![CDATA[
gap> D := CompleteDigraph(IsMutable, 4);
<mutable digraph with 4 vertices, 12 edges>
gap> gv := GraphvizGraph(D);
<graphviz graph "hgn" with 4 nodes and 6 edges>
gap> AsString(gv);
"//dot\ngraph hgn {\n\tnode [shape=circle] \n\t1\n\t2\n\t3\n\t4\n\t2 -\
- 1\n\t3 -- 1\n\t3 -- 2\n\t4 -- 1\n\t4 -- 2\n\t4 -- 3\n}\n"
gap> DigraphRemoveEdge(D, 1, 3);
<mutable digraph with 4 vertices, 11 edges>
gap> gv := GraphvizDigraph(D);
<graphviz digraph "hgn" with 4 nodes and 11 edges>
gap> AsString(gv);
"//dot\ndigraph hgn {\n\tnode [shape=circle] \n\t1\n\t2\n\t3\n\t4\n\t1\
 -> 2\n\t1 -> 4\n\t2 -> 1\n\t2 -> 3\n\t2 -> 4\n\t3 -> 1\n\t3 -> 2\n\t3\
 -> 4\n\t4 -> 1\n\t4 -> 2\n\t4 -> 3\n}\n"
]]></Example>
    </Description>
  </ManSection>
<#/GAPDoc>

<#GAPDoc Label="GraphvizColoredDigraph">
  <ManSection>
    <Oper Name="GraphvizVertexColoredDigraph" Arg="D, colors"/>
    <Oper Name="GraphvizVertexColoredGraph" Arg="D, colors"/>
    <Oper Name="GraphvizEdgeColoredDigraph" Arg="D, colors"/>
    <Oper Name="GraphvizEdgeColoredGraph" Arg="D, colors"/>
    <Oper Name="GraphvizColoredDigraph" Arg="D, vert_colors, edge_colors"/>
    <Oper Name="GraphvizColoredGraph" Arg="D, vert_colors, edge_colors"/>
    <Returns>A &GRAPHVIZFORGAP; object.</Returns>
    <Description>
      These operations produce colored &GRAPHVIZFORGAP; objects representing
      the digraph <A>D</A> according to the specified colors. The variants ending
      in <C>Graph</C> require <A>D</A> to be symmetric.
      For all of these functions valid colors are strings containing:
      <List>
          <Mark>RGB</Mark>
          <Item>
              An RGB color code consisting of 6 hexadecimal digits preceded by
              a <C>#</C>. For example, <C>#ff00ff</C>.
          </Item>
          <Mark>GraphViz 2.4.11 X11 Color Scheme</Mark>
          <Item>
              One of the color strings specified at:
              <URL>http://graphviz.org/doc/info/colors.html</URL>
          </Item>
      </List>

      <C>GraphvizVertexColoredDigraph</C> and <C>GraphvizVertexColoredGraph</C>
      require their argument <A>colors</A> to be a list of length equal to the
      number of vertices of <A>D</A> consisting of strings representing colors
      as described above.
      <P/>

      <C>GraphvizEdgeColoredDigraph</C> and <C>GraphvizEdgeColoredGraph</C>
      require their argument <A>colors</A> to be a list of lists with the same
      shape of the out-neighbours of the digraph <A>D</A> consisting of strings
      representing colors as described above.
      <P/>

      <C>GraphvizColoredDigraph</C> and <C>GraphvizColoredGraph</C> require
      their arguments:
      <List>
          <Mark><A>vert_colors</A></Mark>
          <Item>
            to represent vertex colors as described for
              <C>GraphvizVertexColoredDigraph</C>;
          </Item>
          <Mark><A>edge_colors</A></Mark>
          <Item>
            to represent edge colors as described for
              <C>GraphvizEdgeColoredDigraph</C>;
          </Item>
      </List>

      See the &GRAPHVIZFORGAP; package documentation for more details.
      <P/>

      See also <Ref Func="Splash" BookName="GraphvizForGAP"/>
      <Example><![CDATA[
gap> D := Digraph([[2], [1, 3], [2]]);
<immutable digraph with 3 vertices, 4 edges>
gap> vert_colors := ["blue", "pink", "purple"];;
gap> edge_colors := [["green"], ["green", "red"], ["red"]];;
gap> GraphvizVertexColoredDigraph(D, vert_colors);
<graphviz digraph "hgn" with 3 nodes and 4 edges>
gap> GraphvizVertexColoredGraph(D, vert_colors);
<graphviz graph "hgn" with 3 nodes and 2 edges>
gap> GraphvizEdgeColoredDigraph(D, edge_colors);
<graphviz digraph "hgn" with 3 nodes and 4 edges>
gap> GraphvizEdgeColoredGraph(D, edge_colors);
<graphviz graph "hgn" with 3 nodes and 2 edges>
gap> GraphvizColoredDigraph(D, vert_colors, edge_colors);
<graphviz digraph "hgn" with 3 nodes and 4 edges>
gap> GraphvizColoredGraph(D, vert_colors, edge_colors);
<graphviz graph "hgn" with 3 nodes and 2 edges>
]]></Example>
    </Description>
  </ManSection>
<#/GAPDoc>

<#GAPDoc Label="DotColoredDigraph">
  <ManSection>
    <Oper Name="DotVertexColoredDigraph" Arg="D, colors"/>
    <Oper Name="DotSymmetricVertexColoredDigraph" Arg="D, colors"/>
    <Oper Name="DotEdgeColoredDigraph" Arg="D, colors"/>
    <Oper Name="DotSymmetricEdgeColoredDigraph" Arg="D, colors"/>
    <Oper Name="DotColoredDigraph" Arg="D, vert_colors, edge_colors"/>
    <Oper Name="DotSymmetricColoredDigraph" Arg="D, vert_colors, edge_colors"/>
    <Returns>A string.</Returns>
    <Description>
      <B>WARNING!</B> As of v2.0.0 of &Digraphs; these functions are
      deprecated in favour of the following operations, respectively:
      <List>
        <Item><Ref Oper="GraphvizVertexColoredDigraph"/></Item>
        <Item><Ref Oper="GraphvizVertexColoredGraph"/></Item>
        <Item><Ref Oper="GraphvizEdgeColoredDigraph"/></Item>
        <Item><Ref Oper="GraphvizEdgeColoredGraph"/></Item>
        <Item><Ref Oper="GraphvizColoredDigraph"/></Item>
        <Item><Ref Oper="GraphvizColoredGraph"/></Item>
      </List>
      Each takes the same arguments as its replacement and returns
      <C>AsString</C> applied to the resulting &GRAPHVIZFORGAP; object.
      For example,
      <C>DotColoredDigraph(D, vert_colors, edge_colors)</C> returns
      <C>AsString(GraphvizColoredDigraph(D, vert_colors, edge_colors))</C>.
      The <C>DotSymmetric</C> variants require <A>D</A> to be symmetric.
    </Description>
  </ManSection>
<#/GAPDoc>

<#GAPDoc Label="GraphvizVertexLabelledDigraph">
  <ManSection>
    <Oper Name="GraphvizVertexLabelledDigraph" Arg="D"/>
    <Oper Name="GraphvizVertexLabelledGraph" Arg="D"/>
    <Returns>A &GRAPHVIZFORGAP; object.</Returns>
    <Description>
      These operations produce the same pictures as
      <Ref Oper="GraphvizDigraph"/> and <Ref Oper="GraphvizGraph"/>,
      respectively, using <Ref Oper="DigraphVertexLabels"/> to label the
      vertices instead of their numbers. Labels are converted to strings.
      <C>GraphvizVertexLabelledGraph</C> requires <A>D</A> to be symmetric.
      <P/>

      Use <Ref Oper="SetDigraphVertexLabels"/> to set the vertex labels.
      The resulting object can be displayed using
      <Ref Func="Splash" BookName="GraphvizForGAP"/>.
      <Example><![CDATA[
gap> D := Digraph([[2], [1]]);;
gap> SetDigraphVertexLabels(D, ["left", "right"]);
gap> GraphvizVertexLabelledDigraph(D);
<graphviz digraph "hgn" with 2 nodes and 2 edges>
gap> GraphvizVertexLabelledGraph(D);
<graphviz graph "hgn" with 2 nodes and 1 edge>
]]></Example>
    </Description>
  </ManSection>
<#/GAPDoc>

<#GAPDoc Label="DotVertexLabelledDigraph">
  <ManSection>
    <Oper Name="DotVertexLabelledDigraph" Arg="D"/>
    <Returns>A string.</Returns>
    <Description>
      <B>WARNING!</B> As of v2.0.0 of &Digraphs; this function is
      deprecated in favour of:
      <List>
          <Item><Ref Oper="GraphvizVertexLabelledDigraph"/></Item>
      </List>
      It returns
      <C>AsString(GraphvizVertexLabelledDigraph(<A>D</A>))</C>, using
      <Ref Oper="DigraphVertexLabels"/> as the vertex labels.
    </Description>
  </ManSection>
<#/GAPDoc>

<#GAPDoc Label="GraphvizColoredEdgeLabelledDigraph">
  <ManSection>
    <Oper Name="GraphvizColoredEdgeLabelledDigraph"
          Arg="D, vert_colors, edge_colors, labels"/>
    <Returns>A &GRAPHVIZFORGAP; object.</Returns>
    <Description>
      This operation produces the same picture as
      <Ref Oper="GraphvizColoredDigraph"/>, with labels on the edges.
      The arguments <A>vert_colors</A> and <A>edge_colors</A> specify colors
      as described there. The argument <A>labels</A> must be a list of lists
      with the same shape as <C>OutNeighbours(<A>D</A>)</C>:
      <C>labels[i][j]</C> labels the edge from vertex <C>i</C> to
      <C>OutNeighbours(D)[i][j]</C>.
      <P/>

      See also <Ref Oper="DotEdgeWeightedDigraph"/> for displaying edge
      weights and highlighting a path.
      <Example><![CDATA[
gap> D := Digraph([[2], [3], []]);;
gap> vert_colors := ["blue", "red", "green"];;
gap> edge_colors := [["black"], ["black"], []];;
gap> labels := [[5], [7], []];;
gap> GraphvizColoredEdgeLabelledDigraph(D, vert_colors,
> edge_colors, labels);
<graphviz digraph "hgn" with 3 nodes and 2 edges>
]]></Example>
    </Description>
  </ManSection>
<#/GAPDoc>

<#GAPDoc Label="DotColoredEdgeLabelledDigraph">
  <ManSection>
    <Oper Name="DotColoredEdgeLabelledDigraph"
          Arg="D, vert_colors, edge_colors, labels"/>
    <Returns>A string.</Returns>
    <Description>
      <B>WARNING!</B> As of v2.0.0 of &Digraphs; this function is
      deprecated in favour of:
      <List>
          <Item><Ref Oper="GraphvizColoredEdgeLabelledDigraph"/></Item>
      </List>
      It takes the same arguments and returns
      <C>AsString(GraphvizColoredEdgeLabelledDigraph(D, vert_colors,
      edge_colors, labels))</C>. In particular, both <A>edge_colors</A> and
      <A>labels</A> have the same shape as <C>OutNeighbours(<A>D</A>)</C>.
    </Description>
  </ManSection>
<#/GAPDoc>

<#GAPDoc Label="DotPartialOrderDigraph">
  <ManSection>
    <Attr Name="DotPartialOrderDigraph" Arg="digraph"/>
    <Returns>A string.</Returns>
    <Description>
      <B>WARNING!</B> As of v2.0.0 of &Digraphs; these functions are
